course: dictionary
lesson: 11242
title: Many meanings of world
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word world has several meanings, and the words around it tell you which one you need. Ask yourself what would fit, then try your meaning in the sentence. «China also gave the world porcelain, tea, kites and an early earthquake detector» means everyone on Earth, because it is about gifts to all of humankind.
explain: In science, a world can be a planet, especially one where living things might live. So «other worlds» means other planets. Here the clue is the science lesson, not the word itself.
explain: A world can also be a area of life or activity, like «the world of sport» or «the animal world». The phrase «It did me a world of good» uses world to mean a lot, so it helped me very much. Read the whole phrase, and you will find the meaning.
fact: World means the Earth and everything on it: all countries and all people.
fact: A world can be a planet, especially one where living things might live.
fact: On a globe or world map you can see seven continents and five oceans.
fact: «The natural world» means nature, all the living things and places not made by people.
fact: «Out of this world» means wonderful, and «mean the world to» means matters very much.
exercise: In science Ms Patel says «other worlds» might have living things. What does world mean here? | A kind of sport | A country | *A planet | A map of the seas
exercise: «French also has many varieties around the world, from Paris to Quebec to West Africa.» What does around the world mean here? | *In many places across the Earth | Under the sea | Spinning round and round | Only in one city
exercise: «It did me a world of good.» What does world mean in this phrase? | A planet | A map of the seas | *A lot | The whole Earth
test: Which phrase means nature, all the living things and places not made by people? | A world record | Around the world | *The natural world | Mean the world to
test: How many continents are shown on a world map? | Two | *Seven | Twelve | Five
exam: Which phrase means wonderful? | *Out of this world | Around the world | World record | Mean the world to
